                %li
                  %a{:href => "#openclosed_string_duality"} Open/closed string duality
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} with boundaries
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            with punctures) may typically be read in at least two different ways as describing either a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed string
            or an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
            = succeed "-process." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering"} scattering
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/OpenClosedStringWorldsheetEndingOnBrane.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#Schomerus07"} Schomerus 07, Figure 4
          %p
            But since the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitude"} string scattering amplitude
            is the same no matter which perspective is taken, this exhibits an equivalence (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"}> duality
            ”) between these open- and closed string amplitudes.
          %p
            For example, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            stretching between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolumes"} worldvolumes
            manifestly represents equivalently the following two rather different-seeming
            = succeed "-processes:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering"} string scattering
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed string
                emitted from one of the branes and absorbed by the other;
            %li
              %p
                an open string with ends on both branes going around a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-loop"} 1-loop
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+diagram"} vacuum diagram
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/OpenClosedCylinderWorldsheetEndingOnBranes.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Schomerus07"} Schomerus 07, Figure 4
              %a{:href => "#Peschanski09"} Peschanski 09, Figure 1
          %p Since
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                closed string excitations include
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitons"} gravitons
                inducing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              %p (in the above example: the gravitational attraction between the two branes)
            %li
              %p
                open string excitations include
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluons"} gluons
                inducing the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
                described by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+fields"} Yang-Mills
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
                –e.g. the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
              %p
                (in the above example: the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                gauge field on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coincident+branes"} coincident branes
          %p
            open/closed string duality implies
            %em gauge/gravity duality
            between these different
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theories"} effective field theories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KLT+relations"} KLT relations
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD+correspondence"} AdS/QCD correspondence
            %li
              %p
                the
                %span.newWikiWord
                  gauge-string correspondence
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/gauge-string+correspondence"} ?
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#in_large__limit_and_holography
            In large
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            limit and holography
          %p
            Open/closed string duality plays a subtle role when interpreting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+double+line+notation"} 't Hooft double line notation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
            alternatively as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
            or as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
            (
            %a{:href => "#GopakumarVafa98"}> Gopakumar-Vafa 98
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GaiottoRastelli03"} Gaiotto-Rastelli 03
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gopakumar04"} Gopakumar 04
